---

## Lore

The Spouter is Lemuria''s Master Psychic of water. Where other psychics move objects or minds, a Spouter moves the sea itself: riding a wave with no board, shooting through the depths like a torpedo, turning a puddle or a burst pipe into a weapon. None of it works without water close at hand, and a Spouter caught on a dry prairie or in a desert is badly out of place. Most of them treat that as a dare rather than a weakness.

About half of all Spouters serve in the Lemurian defense force as Spouter Guardsmen, though they are held in less esteem than the Oceanic Guardsmen. A quarter work as scouts and explorers, and the rest turn up as farmers, builders, healers and teachers. On the surface world they have found a calling as vampire hunters, since the undead of the land fear water in a way the undead Milu of the sea do not.

Years spent mastering Hydro-Psionics leave little time for schooling, so a Spouter knows fewer skills than most Lemurians and leans on wits and powers instead. They tend to be quick thinkers who enjoy danger, adapt fast, and play with their abilities as readily as they fight with them. To a Spouter nearly everything is an adventure or a challenge.

## GM Notes

- Powers at level one: the eight traditional psionics, Hold Breath, Hydro-Propulsion and Sense Water are automatic. The player then rolls 1D4+1 for the number of further Hydro-Psionics of choice and takes one Hydro-Super-Psionic. The wizard handles the roll as the "Hydro-Psionics of Choice" pick; use its Roll button.
- Each new level adds one Hydro-Psionic, and levels 3, 5, 8, 10 and 13 add a Hydro-Super-Psionic. There are only fifteen Hydro-Psionics and six Hydro-Super-Psionics, so the lists run out before level fifteen; the book does not say what the spare picks become.
- Every Hydro-Psionic power needs existing water inside its range. Within a mile of a ley line, range and duration rise by half; at a nexus, range, duration and damage double.
- +3 to Perception Rolls involving water and psionics and +1 to parry and dodge while in or using water are conditional and are not added to the sheet.
- The equipment list holds one non-weapon symbiote pick; the book gives 1D4, so roll and add any others by hand. The war steed and the small animal companion are chosen with the G.M. and are not on the equipment list.
